===Verb===
{{en-verb}}<!-- formerly had datumming, datummed as alternatives; too rare -->

# To provide missing data points by using a mathematical model to [[extrapolate]] values that are outside the range of a measuring device.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|title=Model-based Depth Imaging|author=Stuart Fagin|page=164|ISBN=1560800852|passage=On the left the stacking velocity functions are '''datumed''' to sea level and show great disparity.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|title=Practical Seismic Data Analysis|author=Hua-Wei Zhou -|page=62|ISBN=0521199107|passage=On the other hand, if we have a sufficiently accurate near-surface velocity model, we may apply wavefield '''datuming''' to convert the raw data into new data as if they were recorded along a datum below the near surface (Box 2.3).}}

